-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1א', §1.23 שעות גיל למורים וגננות
-- Age hours: the reduction of a teaching employee's position base at 50 and
-- at 55, who is entitled to it, the managers' version, and how salary is
-- computed for those entitled.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `1.23 שעות גיל למורים וגננות`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p1 Amendment note ("this section was amended on 14.1.04").

-- Dates are written as numbers YYYYMMDD (1 September 1978 is 19780901). A
-- school year is named by the calendar year it starts in (5785 = 2024-25 is 2024).
@desc A teaching employee in one school year, as far as section 1.23 asks about it.
DECLARE `age-hours case` HAS
    `school year`                         IS A NUMBER  @desc the calendar year the school year starts in, on 1 September
    `birth year`                          IS A NUMBER
    `full-position base hours`            IS A NUMBER  @desc the weekly hours of a full position before any age reduction, set by the takanon's rules on position bases (an input here)
    `hours worked`                        IS A NUMBER  @desc the weekly hours the employee actually works
    `employed part-time`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `was offered completion of the position and refused` IS A BOOLEAN
    `refused on health grounds confirmed by the district medical committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the district medical committee confirmed that the employee cannot work a full position
    `no full position could be found`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `pensioner employed under section 35 of the pensions law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a pensioner employed in the civil service or a "public fund" under section 35 of the State Service (Pensions) Law 1970
    `mother of a child under 14`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `monthly salary of a full position`   IS A NUMBER  @desc set by the salary scales; an input, never a number of this file

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p2 encodes below: "the number of teaching hours" in this section means the number of hours of the position base, so every reduction is taken off the base (`full-position base hours`).

§§ `1.23 ¶3–¶4 The reduction at 50 and at 55`

-- §1.23.1: reaching 50 "by 31 December" gives the reduction from the start of
-- that school year; reaching it on 1 January or later, from the next one. The
-- school year starting in year Y runs through 31 December of Y, so reaching 50
-- by then means reaching it in calendar year Y or earlier; reaching it from
-- 1 January means reaching it in calendar year Y + 1, and the reduction then
-- starts with the school year Y + 1, which the first rule already gives.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reaches` age `by 31 December of the school year` c IF
    c's `birth year` PLUS age AT MOST c's `school year`

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reaches` age `on 1 January or later in the school year` c IF
    c's `birth year` PLUS age EQUALS c's `school year` PLUS 1

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p3
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reduction for 50` c IS
    IF `reaches` 50 `by 31 December of the school year` c
    THEN 2
    ELSE 0

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p4
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `further reduction for 55` c IS
    IF `reaches` 55 `by 31 December of the school year` c
    THEN 2
    ELSE 0

GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `age hours` c IS `reduction for 50` c PLUS `further reduction for 55` c

§§ `1.23 ¶5–¶9 Who is entitled`

-- §1.23.3א: a part-time employee offered completion of the position who
-- refused it is not entitled to the age-hours reduction.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p5
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not entitled, having refused completion of a part-time position` c IF
    c's `employed part-time` AND c's `was offered completion of the position and refused`

-- §1.23.3ב: notwithstanding 3א, one who refuses on health grounds is
-- entitled, if the district medical committee confirmed that the employee
-- cannot work a full position.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p6
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled notwithstanding the refusal, on health grounds` c IF
    `not entitled, having refused completion of a part-time position` c
    AND c's `refused on health grounds confirmed by the district medical committee`

-- §1.23.4: a part-time employee who could not be given a full position is
-- entitled, and is paid on the hours counted as a full position for an
-- employee of their age (§§1.23.1–2). The same base serves every entitled
-- employee.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p7
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled as a part-timer for whom no full position was found` c IF
    c's `employed part-time` AND c's `no full position could be found`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p7
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `full position for the employee's age` c IS
    c's `full-position base hours` MINUS `age hours` c

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p7
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `position fraction for salary` c IS
    IF `entitled to the age-hours reduction` c
    THEN c's `hours worked` DIVIDED BY `full position for the employee's age` c
    ELSE c's `hours worked` DIVIDED BY c's `full-position base hours`

GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `monthly salary` c IS
    c's `monthly salary of a full position` TIMES `position fraction for salary` c

-- §1.23.5: a pensioner employed in the civil service or a "public fund"
-- under section 35 of the pensions law is entitled.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p8
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled as a pensioner employed under section 35` c IF
    c's `pensioner employed under section 35 of the pensions law`

-- §1.23.6, "notwithstanding §3": a mother of a child under 14, employed
-- part-time for at least 24 hours, has her salary computed with the age
-- hours "if she works 79% of a position". F-1.23-a: read as a floor of the
-- full position for her age (the base less her age hours), it is the reading
-- under which the clause can be met at all.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p9
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled as a mother of a child under 14, notwithstanding section 3` c IF
        c's `mother of a child under 14`
    AND c's `employed part-time`
    AND c's `hours worked` AT LEAST 24
    AND c's `hours worked` AT LEAST 0.79 TIMES `full position for the employee's age` c

§§ `1.23 ¶3–¶9 Entitlement, all paragraphs together`

-- Paragraphs 1–2 give the reduction by age; 3א takes it away from a
-- part-timer who refused completion; 3ב, 4, 5 and 6 each give it back.
@export default Whether a teaching employee is entitled to the age-hours reduction in a school year, under section 1.23 of the takanon
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case` @desc the employee and the school year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the age-hours reduction` c IF
        `age hours` c GREATER THAN 0
    AND (   (NOT `not entitled, having refused completion of a part-time position` c)
         OR `entitled as a part-timer for whom no full position was found` c
         OR `entitled notwithstanding the refusal, on health grounds` c
         OR `entitled as a mother of a child under 14, notwithstanding section 3` c
         OR `entitled as a pensioner employed under section 35` c)

-- F-1.23-a: "works 79% of a position" read as an exact figure can never be
-- met together with "at least 24 hours" for a base of up to 30 hours (24 is
-- already more than 79% of 30), and read as a floor it adds nothing to the
-- 24 hours there. Shown here for bases from 24 to 30 weekly hours.
`exactly 79% of a base of up to 30 hours is fewer than 24 hours` MEANS
    all (GIVEN b YIELD 0.79 TIMES b LESS THAN 24) (LIST 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 29, 30)
#ASSERT `exactly 79% of a base of up to 30 hours is fewer than 24 hours`

`at least 24 hours already exceeds 79% of a base of up to 30 hours` MEANS
    all (GIVEN b YIELD 24 AT LEAST 0.79 TIMES b) (LIST 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 29, 30)
#ASSERT `at least 24 hours already exceeds 79% of a base of up to 30 hours`

§§ `1.23 ¶10–¶11 Age hours for principals, coordinators and deputy principals`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p10 Sub-heading ("age hours for principals, coordinators and deputy principals").

@desc A full-time principal, deputy principal or coordinator, as far as the managers' paragraph asks about them.
DECLARE `manager's case` HAS
    `manager's school year`             IS A NUMBER @desc the calendar year the school year starts in
    `manager's birth year`              IS A NUMBER
    `employed in a full position`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `teaching hours in classes`         IS A NUMBER @desc weekly hours the manager teaches in classes
    `manager's full-position hours`     IS A NUMBER @desc the weekly hours of the manager's full position (an input)

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p11
GIVEN m IS A `manager's case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `managers' weekly reduction` m IS
    IF NOT m's `employed in a full position`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `teaching share` TIMES
             (BRANCH IF m's `manager's birth year` PLUS 55 AT MOST m's `manager's school year` THEN 4
                     IF m's `manager's birth year` PLUS 50 AT MOST m's `manager's school year` THEN 2
                     OTHERWISE 0)
    WHERE
        `teaching share` MEANS
            IF m's `teaching hours in classes` AT LEAST (2 DIVIDED BY 3) TIMES m's `manager's full-position hours`
            THEN 1
            ELSE 0.5

§§ `1.23 ¶12–¶15 General`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p12 Sub-heading ("general").

-- §§1.23 general 1א, 1ב and 2: from 1.9.78 an entitled employee working above
-- the full position is paid for every hour on the age-hours base, except
-- substitution hours, which are paid "as usual" (on the unreduced base);
-- from 1.9.80 the words excepting substitution hours are deleted.
DECLARE `kind of hour above the position` IS ONE OF
    `an extra hour`
    `a substitution hour`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p13 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p14 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p15
GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`, k IS A `kind of hour above the position`, `date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours of the base an hour above the position is paid on` c k `date` IS
    IF     `entitled to the age-hours reduction` c
       AND `date` AT LEAST 19780901
       AND NOT (k EQUALS `a substitution hour` AND `date` LESS THAN 19800901)
    THEN `full position for the employee's age` c
    ELSE c's `full-position base hours`

GIVEN c IS AN `age-hours case`, k IS A `kind of hour above the position`, `date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `value of a weekly hour above the position` c k `date` IS
    c's `monthly salary of a full position` DIVIDED BY `hours of the base an hour above the position is paid on` c k `date`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p16 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p17 Source list: circulars and the education-law compilation the section rests on.
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p18 Source list: Director-General's circulars.
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p19 Source list: a circular and a deputy director-general's letter.
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p20 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_23__ssec_1_23/p21 Source list: a Director-General's circular.

-- Worked examples. The 30-hour base and the salary of 10,000 are placeholders,
-- not figures of the takanon. Cases are written positionally, in the order of
-- the record's fields: school year, birth year, base hours, hours worked,
-- part-time, offered completion and refused, health exception confirmed, no
-- full position found, section-35 pensioner, mother of a child under 14, salary.
`a teacher of 52 in a full position` MEANS
    `age-hours case` 2024 1972 30 28 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10000

#ASSERT `age hours` `a teacher of 52 in a full position` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `entitled to the age-hours reduction` `a teacher of 52 in a full position`
#ASSERT `monthly salary` `a teacher of 52 in a full position` EQUALS 10000

-- Born in 1975, the teacher reaches 50 during 2025: in the school year that
-- starts in 2024 the birthday falls after 1 January, so the reduction starts in 2025.
`a teacher who turns 50 in the spring` MEANS
    `age-hours case` 2024 1975 30 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10000
`the same teacher a year later` MEANS
    `age-hours case` 2025 1975 30 28 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10000
#ASSERT `reaches` 50 `on 1 January or later in the school year` `a teacher who turns 50 in the spring`
#ASSERT `age hours` `a teacher who turns 50 in the spring` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `age hours` `the same teacher a year later` EQUALS 2

-- A part-time teacher of 56 who refused completion loses the reduction,
-- unless the district medical committee confirmed the health ground.
`a part-timer of 56 who refused completion` MEANS
    `age-hours case` 2024 1968 30 20 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10000
`a part-timer of 56 who refused on confirmed health grounds` MEANS
    `age-hours case` 2024 1968 30 20 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10000
#ASSERT `age hours` `a part-timer of 56 who refused completion` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT NOT `entitled to the age-hours reduction` `a part-timer of 56 who refused completion`
#ASSERT `entitled to the age-hours reduction` `a part-timer of 56 who refused on confirmed health grounds`

-- Section 1.23.6: a mother of a child under 14 who refused completion, at 24 of the 26 hours for her age.
`a mother of 56 working 24 hours` MEANS
    `age-hours case` 2024 1968 30 24 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 10000
#ASSERT `entitled to the age-hours reduction` `a mother of 56 working 24 hours`

-- Section 1.23.4: no full position found, 13 hours of the 26-hour base for 56: half a position.
`a part-timer of 56 with no full position found` MEANS
    `age-hours case` 2024 1968 30 13 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 10000
#ASSERT `monthly salary` `a part-timer of 56 with no full position found` EQUALS 5000

`a principal of 56 teaching 20 of 30 hours` MEANS
    `manager's case` WITH
        `manager's school year`         IS 2024
        `manager's birth year`          IS 1968
        `employed in a full position`   IS TRUE
        `teaching hours in classes`     IS 20
        `manager's full-position hours` IS 30
`a principal of 56 teaching 10 of 30 hours` MEANS
    `manager's case` 2024 1968 TRUE 10 30
#ASSERT `managers' weekly reduction` `a principal of 56 teaching 20 of 30 hours` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `managers' weekly reduction` `a principal of 56 teaching 10 of 30 hours` EQUALS 2

-- An extra hour is paid on the 28-hour age base; a substitution hour before 1.9.80 on the 30-hour base.
#ASSERT `hours of the base an hour above the position is paid on` `a teacher of 52 in a full position` `an extra hour` 19790101 EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `hours of the base an hour above the position is paid on` `a teacher of 52 in a full position` `a substitution hour` 19790101 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `hours of the base an hour above the position is paid on` `a teacher of 52 in a full position` `a substitution hour` 19810101 EQUALS 28
